# Copy this file to .env.local (dev) and fill in real values. .env.local is
# gitignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# These two are PUBLIC by design (they ship inside the browser bundle; access
# control is enforced by Postgres Row-Level Security, not by keeping this
# secret). Get them from: Supabase Dashboard -> Settings -> API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# ── Optional: T0-3 RLS regression suite (src/test/rls.integration.test.ts) ──
# Tier 1 (anonymous-access checks) runs automatically once the two vars above
# are set. Tier 2 additionally needs a DEDICATED, low-privilege `sales`-role
# test account created for this purpose only — never a real staff login.
# Put these in .env.test.local instead of .env.local (both are gitignored via
# the `*.local` pattern), so they aren't loaded outside test runs.
#   VITE_RLS_TEST_SALES_EMAIL=
#   VITE_RLS_TEST_SALES_PASSWORD=

# ── Optional: T0-7 Playwright E2E suite (e2e/*.spec.ts, see e2e/README.md) ──
# These are PLAIN env vars, not VITE_-prefixed — Playwright's test runner
# doesn't go through Vite. Put them in .env.test.local too. The sales account
# can be the same one used above (just repeated under this different name).
# Never a real staff login for any of these.
#   E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL=
#   E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
#   E2E_SALES_EMAIL=
#   E2E_SALES_PASSWORD=
#   E2E_ENGINEER_EMAIL=
#   E2E_ENGINEER_PASSWORD=
